From 9d49315a0367f2f073c5eef7a8b22e894441147a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:08:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 196/240] Bugfix: compute torus arc count from the neighbor
 mask in `gmk_m2` [report R. Perry]

The closed-form arc count of 8-neighbor tori subtracted the arcs
removed along each dimension independently, so that arcs removed
for both dimensions were subtracted twice when both dimensions are
smaller than 3. The header of tori of sizes 1x1, 1x2, 2x1 and 2x2
did not match the arcs written, and the files could not be loaded.
Since all vertices of a torus have the same neighbor mask, compute
it once and derive the arc count from it, as the arcs are written.

Refs: CLI-18
